From bc33e3e8401eec4b0e4994bd6971daba751212fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sukrit Jaidee <45908411+SukritJaAIproject@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 15:41:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] build(desktop): overridable product identity for side-by-side
 editions

Let a second edition of the desktop app be built from the same tree and
installed next to the current line as its own Windows application:

- IMPS_PRODUCT_NAME / IMPS_APP_ID override build.productName / build.appId
  (window title, shortcut, <name>.exe, uninstall entry, artifact names
  <slug>-Offline-Setup-<version>.exe / <slug>-Online-Setup-<version>.exe);
  IMPS_RESOURCES_ROOT reuses the resources of an earlier unpacked build.
- main.cjs reads the product name from the package.json baked into the
  asar, so each edition gets its own %APPDATA% folder for logs and jobs.
- build-installers.mjs derives its artifact names and the prepackaged
  executable name from the same product name.
- When signing is on, every executable under the bundled Wireshark
  directory (including extcap\) is listed as a "!name" entry in
  win.signExts so electron-builder no longer replaces the Wireshark
  Foundation signature with ours.
- README: Editions section with the recipe used for
  "iMPS Fault Detection Snapshot 2026-09-12" (App ID
  th.co.imps.faultdetection.snapshot20260912, version 1.1.0).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
